{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Go forth from the ark, you and your wife.</b> Now at their entry he mentioned the males separately and the females separately — this was so that they would not breed and multiply in the ark, for otherwise there is reason to fear that all the other animals would learn from them and breed and multiply in the ark, and then the ark would not hold them, for it was made only with the exact measure for all who would enter it. And should you say that even those who entered there stood by way of miracle, in any case why would the Holy One, blessed be He, perform a miracle for no need — especially for those who do not suffer at a time when the whole world is immersed in suffering?" "And as for what is said also regarding the departure, ״וַיֵּצֵא נֹחַ וּבָנָיו וְאִשְׁתּוֹ וּנְשֵׁי בָנָיו״ (Genesis 8:18) — even though the Holy One, blessed be He, permitted relations to Noah, he did not accept it upon himself, for he said: lest they continue to sin and the waters of the Flood come and sweep them away, and why should I beget in vain and to no purpose? Until HaShem swore not to bring the waters of the Flood again — then it was said ״פְּרוּ וּרְבוּ״ etc. (Genesis 9:1). And Noah wanted first to bring an offering before engaging in propagation. And according to the plain sense we may say that at Noah's entry into the ark, even yichud with his wife was forbidden to him, for to this end it says ״וּבָאתָ אֶל הַתֵּבָה אַתָּה וּבָנֶיךָ״ etc. (Genesis 6:18). And at the departure, He did not yet permit him relations but only yichud was permitted to him, for this is what is understood from the statement ״צֵא מִן הַתֵּבָה אַתָּה וְאִשְׁתְּךָ״ (Genesis 8:16). And since relations were not permitted to him but only yichud alone, Noah therefore added of his own accord and forbade upon himself even yichud — ״וַיֵּצֵא מִן הַתֵּבָה נֹחַ וּבָנָיו״ (Genesis 8:18) — until he was told explicitly ״פְּרוּ וּרְבוּ״ (Genesis 9:1), then everything was permitted to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:27:42.933105611Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}